  "findings": [
    "The official Survey of India index lists 27 state/UT village-boundary archives. The latest acquisition downloaded and audited 14 of 27; 13 remain unavailable in this run.",
    "The latest run contains 71,484 village administrative features and 37 invalid geometries across the 14 archives.",
    "The missing archives are Andhra Pradesh, Bihar, Chhattisgarh, Gujarat, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Odisha, Punjab, Rajasthan, Tamil Nadu, Uttar Pradesh and West Bengal. Madhya Pradesh's source archive advertises 280,668,854 bytes and exceeded the 150 MiB per-file limit.",
    "Telangana's source metadata claims WKID 3857 while its .prj declares custom LCC_WGS84, so that file's CRS metadata remains unresolved.",
    "These are village administrative boundaries, not Assembly Constituency polygons; many rows have null or repeated Vill_LGD codes and must not be deduplicated without explicit identity/topology rules.",
    "The official ECI statistical-report index did not yield a crawlable state/year link inventory in this run; the five guessed ECI result JavaScript endpoints returned 404, so no national official AC geometry was promoted.",
    "Census 2011 population linkage still requires the authoritative village-code crosswalk and a valid village population table; no constituency population estimate is inferred from these files alone."
  ],
  "decision": "Use acquired files only as source-audited village administrative geometry candidates. Do not insert into the runtime or canonical AC geometry registry until full national coverage, per-file CRS, LGD identity, topology and effective-date checks pass.",
